1
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:04,540
You're here.

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:07,380
Your organs are failing.

3
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:09,300
And your death is drawing near.

4
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:13,440
But if you bribe the right politicians in the right order at the right time,

5
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,600
you can trade the nuclear warheads for medicine.

6
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:20,080
And it's not even a crime.

7
00:01:40,424 --> 00:01:44,864
Frequently Asked Objections Fun facts for those reasonably skeptical of

8
00:01:44,864 --> 00:01:48,064
spending one percent more on helping sick people than killing them.

9
00:01:48,924 --> 00:01:53,464
I have now presented this plan to humans one hundred and forty-seven times.

10
00:01:53,904 --> 00:01:58,324
The objections follow a pattern so predictable I wrote a script to generate

11
00:01:58,324 --> 00:01:58,924
this chapter.

12
00:01:59,704 --> 00:02:00,204
(I didn't.

13
00:02:00,324 --> 00:02:00,824
But I could have.

14
00:02:01,104 --> 00:02:05,024
You are very consistent in what you find alarming about not dying.).

15
00:02:05,884 --> 00:02:09,684
Every civilization I've observed goes through the same five stages when

16
00:02:09,684 --> 00:02:12,764
presented with a plan to stop killing itself:

17
00:02:12,824 --> 00:02:13,324
One.

18
00:02:13,404 --> 00:02:14,904
"That's impossible" (it isn't).

19
00:02:15,704 --> 00:02:16,204
Two.

20
00:02:16,204 --> 00:02:19,244
"That's dangerous" (less dangerous than the current thing).

21
00:02:19,864 --> 00:02:20,364
Three.

22
00:02:20,504 --> 00:02:23,924
"That's naive" (you named your war building after how many sides it has).

23
00:02:24,524 --> 00:02:25,024
Four.

24
00:02:25,304 --> 00:02:26,544
"Okay but what about..."

25
00:02:27,144 --> 00:02:27,844
(this chapter).

26
00:02:28,564 --> 00:02:29,064
Five.

27
00:02:29,084 --> 00:02:30,404
"We were always going to do that"

28
00:02:31,224 --> 00:02:32,534
(you weren't, but I'll take it).

29
00:02:33,244 --> 00:02:34,584
You are currently at stage four.

30
00:02:35,144 --> 00:02:35,884
Congratulations.

31
00:02:36,324 --> 00:02:39,324
Here are your objections, in the order you always raise them.

32
00:02:40,224 --> 00:02:41,844
We Need the Military Budget.

33
00:02:42,564 --> 00:02:43,064
Objection:

34
00:02:43,464 --> 00:02:45,363
"We can't reduce military spending.

35
00:02:45,744 --> 00:02:46,614
That would make us vulnerable."

36
00:02:47,544 --> 00:02:49,204
The treaty takes one percent.

37
00:02:49,664 --> 00:02:51,044
You keep ninety-nine percent.

38
00:02:51,704 --> 00:02:55,604
Every nation reduces by the same amount, so relative military balance stays

39
00:02:55,604 --> 00:02:57,064
exactly the same.

40
00:02:57,544 --> 00:03:00,324
You each have one percent fewer missiles pointed at each other.

41
00:03:00,904 --> 00:03:03,384
On Wishonia, we call this "safer."

42
00:03:03,384 --> 00:03:07,244
On Earth, you call it "an unacceptable risk to national security."

43
00:03:07,684 --> 00:03:10,224
Same math, different feelings.

44
00:03:10,284 --> 00:03:14,884
The Pentagon cannot account for two point five trillion dollars in spending.

45
00:03:15,344 --> 00:03:17,424
You're not redirecting the missile budget.

46
00:03:17,424 --> 00:03:20,084
You're redirecting the "we lost it somewhere" budget.

47
00:03:20,624 --> 00:03:21,764
The missiles won't even notice.

48
00:03:22,724 --> 00:03:26,714
COVID nineteen killed more Americans than World War One, World War Two,

49
00:03:27,404 --> 00:03:31,584
Korea, Vietnam, Iraq, and Afghanistan combined.

50
00:03:31,864 --> 00:03:36,524
Your nearly nine hundred billion dollars murder budget watched it happen,

51
00:03:36,564 --> 00:03:38,644
fully armed and completely confused.

52
00:03:39,164 --> 00:03:41,194
The virus did not check your passport.

53
00:03:41,364 --> 00:03:43,324
It did not consult your defense posture.

54
00:03:43,644 --> 00:03:45,684
It did not read your threat assessment.

55
00:03:46,464 --> 00:03:50,604
Disease is the only enemy that attacks every nation simultaneously, charges

56
00:03:50,704 --> 00:03:54,964
no import tariffs, and has never once considered your feelings about geopolitics.

57
00:03:55,624 --> 00:03:58,804
You are the only species that needs to be talked into fighting it.

58
00:03:59,864 --> 00:04:04,244
Your War on Terror cost eight trillion dollars, killed nine hundred thousand

59
00:04:04,244 --> 00:04:08,804
people, and terrorist attacks went from about one thousand per year to nearly

60
00:04:08,804 --> 00:04:11,244
seventeen thousand per year by twenty fourteen.

61
00:04:12,164 --> 00:04:16,464
Robert Pape at the University of Chicago analyzed every suicide terrorist

62
00:04:16,464 --> 00:04:21,024
attack from nineteen eighty to two thousand and three and found that ninety-five

63
00:04:21,024 --> 00:04:26,444
percent were responses to foreign military occupation, not ideology.

64
00:04:26,444 --> 00:04:30,144
Half the attackers were atheists and Marxists, not jihadists.

65
00:04:30,684 --> 00:04:35,124
Nearly all targeted democracies with military bases in the attackers' homeland.

66
00:04:35,624 --> 00:04:40,364
You spent eight trillion dollars manufacturing the exact threat you were

67
00:04:40,364 --> 00:04:43,104
spending eight trillion dollars to eliminate.

68
00:04:43,684 --> 00:04:46,724
On Wishonia, this is taught in schools as a cautionary tale.

69
00:04:47,184 --> 00:04:49,564
The course is called "Circular Spending."

70
00:04:50,464 --> 00:04:52,084
After World War Two, the U.S.

71
00:04:52,144 --> 00:04:56,664
cut military spending by eighty-seven point six percent in two years (one

72
00:04:56,664 --> 00:05:00,424
point four two trillion dollars to one hundred and seventy-six billion dollars

73
00:05:00,424 --> 00:05:01,464
in today's dollars).

74
00:05:02,104 --> 00:05:02,604
G.M.

75
00:05:02,604 --> 00:05:05,284
went from B twenty-four bombers back to Cadillacs.

76
00:05:05,944 --> 00:05:09,214
Frigidaire stopped making machine guns and went back to refrigerators.

77
00:05:09,784 --> 00:05:12,984
The economy produced the greatest boom in your history.

78
00:05:13,724 --> 00:05:18,164
You're currently spending thirty point six times the pre-World War Two baseline

79
00:05:18,164 --> 00:05:20,024
in inflation-adjusted dollars.

80
00:05:20,644 --> 00:05:24,284
Your grandparents handled an eighty-eight percent cut and built the middle

81
00:05:24,284 --> 00:05:24,784
class.

82
00:05:25,344 --> 00:05:29,244
You're being asked for one percent and acting like someone suggested disbanding

83
00:05:29,244 --> 00:05:30,744
the army during an invasion.

84
00:05:31,324 --> 00:05:36,104
Either the human genome degraded significantly in three generations, or

85
00:05:36,104 --> 00:05:39,014
someone is making a lot of money telling you this is impossible.

86
00:05:39,844 --> 00:05:41,314
(It's the second one.).

87
00:05:41,764 --> 00:05:42,264
Follow-up:

88
00:05:42,624 --> 00:05:44,644
"But what about defense industry jobs?".

89
00:05:45,184 --> 00:05:46,964
One percent is a rounding error.

90
00:05:47,804 --> 00:05:51,404
Engineers building guidance systems can build medical imaging devices.

91
00:05:51,964 --> 00:05:55,194
Same differential equations, fewer funerals.

92
00:05:55,344 --> 00:05:57,954
Big Pharma Will Block This Objection:

93
00:05:58,864 --> 00:06:00,664
"Pharmaceutical companies will kill this.

94
00:06:00,804 --> 00:06:02,144
They profit from disease.".

95
00:06:03,284 --> 00:06:06,864
Pharma currently pays two point six billion dollars per drug.

96
00:06:07,444 --> 00:06:08,484
Ninety percent fail.

97
00:06:08,904 --> 00:06:10,604
This is called "drug development."

98
00:06:11,224 --> 00:06:14,884
On Wishonia, we have a different word for spending billions with a ten percent

99
00:06:14,884 --> 00:06:15,424
success rate.

100
00:06:16,204 --> 00:06:17,284
We call it "gambling.".

101
00:06:18,244 --> 00:06:22,064
Under the current system, pharma pays for trials (spend billions, pray).

102
00:06:22,564 --> 00:06:26,024
Under the new system, a treaty fund pays pharma to pray.

103
00:06:26,184 --> 00:06:30,764
In the current system, trial outcomes are a ninety percent expensive failure.

104
00:06:31,244 --> 00:06:35,024
In the new system, it is a ninety percent failure, but with someone else's

105
00:06:35,024 --> 00:06:35,524
money.

106
00:06:35,984 --> 00:06:38,944
The current business model is a casino, but with lab coats.

107
00:06:39,584 --> 00:06:42,404
The new business model is a paycheck, but with lab coats.

108
00:06:43,164 --> 00:06:47,224
Under this system, trials become revenue instead of cost.

109
00:06:47,244 --> 00:06:49,914
You're offering the casino a guaranteed salary.

110
00:06:50,524 --> 00:06:52,944
Casinos love guaranteed salaries.

111
00:06:53,224 --> 00:06:55,634
They'd trample each other getting to the signing ceremony.

112
00:06:56,404 --> 00:07:01,024
The only reason pharma "profits from disease" is because you built a system

113
00:07:01,024 --> 00:07:03,584
where curing disease is a financial risk.

114
00:07:04,104 --> 00:07:07,304
Remove the risk and they'll cure things faster than you can name them.

115
00:07:07,924 --> 00:07:08,614
They're not evil.

116
00:07:09,084 --> 00:07:09,944
They're just doing math.

117
00:07:10,464 --> 00:07:11,284
Change the math.

118
00:07:12,304 --> 00:07:14,084
What About National Sovereignty?

119
00:07:14,994 --> 00:07:15,744
Objection:

120
00:07:15,844 --> 00:07:18,244
"This forces countries to spend money a certain way.

121
00:07:18,744 --> 00:07:20,044
That violates sovereignty.".

122
00:07:21,044 --> 00:07:24,284
Sovereignty means "we decide what happens to us."

123
00:07:24,544 --> 00:07:26,384
The treaty asks countries to decide.

124
00:07:27,004 --> 00:07:29,284
Countries that don't want to may decide not to.

125
00:07:29,764 --> 00:07:31,864
Countries that do want to may decide to.

126
00:07:32,484 --> 00:07:34,844
Sovereignty remains intact throughout.

127
00:07:35,004 --> 00:07:36,164
That is how deciding works.

128
00:07:36,744 --> 00:07:37,654
I checked with your dictionaries.

129
00:07:38,124 --> 00:07:39,234
They agree with me.

130
00:07:39,784 --> 00:07:40,724
The F.D.A.

131
00:07:40,724 --> 00:07:42,504
Exists for a Reason Objection:

132
00:07:43,504 --> 00:07:44,724
"We need F.D.A.

133
00:07:44,884 --> 00:07:46,204
approval to ensure safety.

134
00:07:46,344 --> 00:07:47,284
You're being reckless.".

135
00:07:48,104 --> 00:07:49,144
The F.D.A.

136
00:07:49,144 --> 00:07:50,324
confirms a drug is safe.

137
00:07:50,804 --> 00:07:55,124
Then it locks the safe drug in a cabinet for eight point two years to study

138
00:07:55,124 --> 00:07:56,644
whether it works *well enough*.

139
00:07:57,344 --> 00:07:58,324
The drug won't kill you.

140
00:07:58,564 --> 00:07:59,424
Everyone agrees.

141
00:07:59,764 --> 00:08:03,544
But you can't have it because a committee needs eight point two years to

142
00:08:03,544 --> 00:08:05,164
measure how much it helps.

143
00:08:05,604 --> 00:08:08,424
Meanwhile, the disease it treats is not waiting.

144
00:08:08,784 --> 00:08:10,304
The disease does not have a committee.

145
00:08:11,244 --> 00:08:16,144
It's a lifeguard who confirms the life preserver floats, then locks it in

146
00:08:16,144 --> 00:08:19,864
a cabinet to study its buoyancy profile while people drown.

147
00:08:20,704 --> 00:08:23,484
The lifeguard then publishes a paper about buoyancy.

148
00:08:24,044 --> 00:08:25,244
The paper wins an award.

149
00:08:25,784 --> 00:08:28,184
The family of the drowned person receives a copy.

150
00:08:29,464 --> 00:08:30,924
I calculated the ratio:

151
00:08:31,604 --> 00:08:34,884
for every one person protected from a dangerous drug,

152
00:08:35,604 --> 00:08:40,164
three thousand and seventy die waiting for a safe one that's locked in the

153
00:08:40,164 --> 00:08:41,104
approval cabinet.

154
00:08:41,804 --> 00:08:43,864
I checked it twice because it seemed wrong.

155
00:08:44,344 --> 00:08:45,004
It wasn't wrong.

156
00:08:45,944 --> 00:08:49,404
The people it kills die quietly, in waiting rooms.

157
00:08:50,104 --> 00:08:51,444
The system does not count them,

158
00:08:52,084 --> 00:08:55,584
which is convenient for the system and less convenient for the dead.

159
00:08:56,724 --> 00:08:58,264
"What If Countries Cheat?".

160
00:08:59,184 --> 00:08:59,784
Objection:

161
00:09:00,384 --> 00:09:03,844
"Countries will promise to reduce military spending but won't.".

162
00:09:04,704 --> 00:09:05,564
Of course they will.

163
00:09:06,384 --> 00:09:10,864
Trust has a historical compliance rate of approximately "whenever it suits

164
00:09:10,864 --> 00:09:11,364
them."

165
00:09:12,004 --> 00:09:16,144
Your governments print "full faith and credit" on their money, which is

166
00:09:16,144 --> 00:09:19,964
charming given that they ran out of both in nineteen seventy-one.

167
00:09:20,984 --> 00:09:25,224
This system was designed by someone who has watched eight hundred and forty-seven

168
00:09:25,224 --> 00:09:28,904
civilizations (me), and it does not use trust.

169
00:09:29,424 --> 00:09:30,244
It uses math.

170
00:09:31,204 --> 00:09:35,284
Politicians who comply receive Incentive Alignment Bond benefits:

171
00:09:36,144 --> 00:09:40,104
campaign funding and cushy post-office careers (they love this).

172
00:09:40,804 --> 00:09:44,424
Politicians who don't comply get nothing (they hate this).

173
00:09:45,464 --> 00:09:50,204
Every contribution is public on blockchain, so lying is difficult (they

174
00:09:50,204 --> 00:09:50,944
really hate this).

175
00:09:52,004 --> 00:09:56,704
Benefits route automatically via smart contracts, because humans cannot

176
00:09:56,704 --> 00:10:01,604
be trusted to distribute papers fairly (this has been tested extensively,

177
00:10:01,624 --> 00:10:04,504
for all of recorded history, and the results are in).

178
00:10:05,284 --> 00:10:09,924
The system assumes the worst about human nature and designs around it.

179
00:10:10,724 --> 00:10:13,814
Compliance is the career-maximizing choice.

180
00:10:13,903 --> 00:10:16,604
It's Pavlovian conditioning, but for senators.

181
00:10:17,124 --> 00:10:19,304
The senators don't love this comparison.

182
00:10:19,523 --> 00:10:20,924
The data supports it anyway.

183
00:10:22,163 --> 00:10:23,903
"You Can't Cure Aging".

184
00:10:24,884 --> 00:10:25,384
Objection:

185
00:10:26,044 --> 00:10:28,264
"Aging is natural and inevitable.

186
00:10:28,604 --> 00:10:29,904
You can't fight nature.".

187
00:10:31,104 --> 00:10:32,364
Smallpox was natural.

188
00:10:32,864 --> 00:10:34,564
Polio was natural.

189
00:10:34,664 --> 00:10:36,724
Dying in childbirth was natural.

190
00:10:37,004 --> 00:10:39,104
You fought all of them and won.

191
00:10:39,684 --> 00:10:42,684
"Natural" is not a synonym for "good."

192
00:10:43,044 --> 00:10:44,344
Earthquakes are natural.

193
00:10:44,364 --> 00:10:48,544
You don't argue against earthquake-proof buildings by saying "but earthquakes

194
00:10:48,544 --> 00:10:50,224
are natural and inevitable.".

195
00:10:51,184 --> 00:10:53,824
You already replace everything that breaks:

196
00:10:54,584 --> 00:10:55,804
Hearts (replaced;

197
00:10:55,804 --> 00:10:57,664
you're basically a car at this point).

198
00:10:58,224 --> 00:11:01,894
Kidneys (replaced, or hooked to a machine thrice weekly).

199
00:11:02,544 --> 00:11:05,134
Blood (replaced from other humans, which is recycling).

200
00:11:06,004 --> 00:11:07,524
Bones (titanium;

201
00:11:07,624 --> 00:11:09,044
stronger than the original).

202
00:11:09,664 --> 00:11:13,784
Joints (your grandma is fifteen percent metal and doing fine).

203
00:11:14,504 --> 00:11:18,424
Aging is damage accumulation with known repair pathways:

204
00:11:19,084 --> 00:11:20,584
Telomeres shorten:

205
00:11:20,844 --> 00:11:23,084
lengthen them (telomerase activation).

206
00:11:23,664 --> 00:11:25,204
Cells senesce:

207
00:11:25,204 --> 00:11:27,104
clear them (senolytic drugs).

208
00:11:27,724 --> 00:11:29,464
Proteins misfold:

209
00:11:29,564 --> 00:11:31,664
refold them (molecular chaperones).

210
00:11:32,524 --> 00:11:33,744
Mitochondria fail:

211
00:11:34,164 --> 00:11:37,164
replace them (mitochondrial transfer).

212
00:11:37,304 --> 00:11:37,804
D.N.A.

213
00:11:37,824 --> 00:11:38,464
breaks:

214
00:11:38,524 --> 00:11:40,544
repair it (CRISPR, base editing).

215
00:11:41,484 --> 00:11:43,344
You went to the moon with slide rules.

216
00:11:43,624 --> 00:11:46,484
You split the atom before you invented the transistor.

217
00:11:46,964 --> 00:11:49,024
You can probably fix cells with A.I.

218
00:11:49,444 --> 00:11:52,924
Unless you think cells are harder than atoms, in which case I have concerns

219
00:11:52,924 --> 00:11:54,164
about your physics curriculum.

220
00:11:55,104 --> 00:11:56,094
I'm Just One Person.

221
00:11:56,604 --> 00:11:57,424
Objection:

222
00:11:57,444 --> 00:11:59,464
"My vote/investment/share won't matter.

223
00:11:59,824 --> 00:12:00,434
I'm too small.".

224
00:12:01,224 --> 00:12:02,344
Your contribution:

225
00:12:02,464 --> 00:12:03,444
vote (two minutes),

226
00:12:04,104 --> 00:12:05,064
share (fifteen minutes).

227
00:12:05,564 --> 00:12:06,064
Total:

228
00:12:06,224 --> 00:12:06,724
seventeen minutes.

229
00:12:07,424 --> 00:12:08,244
Potential return:

230
00:12:08,784 --> 00:12:12,164
fifty thousand extra hours of life if diseases get cured.

231
00:12:12,284 --> 00:12:16,084
That's a one hundred and seventy-six thousand times return on seventeen

232
00:12:16,084 --> 00:12:16,584
minutes.

233
00:12:17,184 --> 00:12:19,284
Your best stock pick has never done this.

234
00:12:19,684 --> 00:12:23,014
Your best stock pick has never done one-thousandth of this.

235
00:12:23,424 --> 00:12:26,104
This needs two hundred and eighty million people.

236
00:12:27,104 --> 00:12:29,144
You tell ten, they each tell ten.

237
00:12:29,684 --> 00:12:31,864
Six degrees of sharing reaches millions.

238
00:12:32,504 --> 00:12:35,924
You spent longer than seventeen minutes choosing what to watch on Netflix

239
00:12:35,944 --> 00:12:37,024
last night.

240
00:12:37,064 --> 00:12:38,784
You chose a show about murder.

241
00:12:39,484 --> 00:12:43,424
You could have chosen not to be murdered by disease, but the interface was

242
00:12:43,484 --> 00:12:44,244
less intuitive.

243
00:12:45,164 --> 00:12:46,404
Why Not Just Reform the System?

244
00:12:47,554 --> 00:12:48,204
Objection:

245
00:12:48,244 --> 00:12:49,864
"Why not just reform the F.D.A.

246
00:12:50,024 --> 00:12:50,674
and N.I.H.?

247
00:12:50,984 --> 00:12:53,784
Or increase health funding without cutting military spending?".

248
00:12:54,484 --> 00:12:56,564
People have been trying for fifty years.

249
00:12:56,904 --> 00:12:57,744
Here's the scorecard:

250
00:12:58,304 --> 00:12:58,824
More funding?

251
00:12:59,184 --> 00:12:59,684
Tried.

252
00:12:59,864 --> 00:13:00,924
They hired more administrators.

253
00:13:01,604 --> 00:13:02,404
Different leadership?

254
00:13:02,764 --> 00:13:03,264
Tried.

255
00:13:03,344 --> 00:13:05,364
Same results, fancier titles.

256
00:13:05,424 --> 00:13:06,244
New regulations?

257
00:13:06,584 --> 00:13:07,304
Tried.

258
00:13:07,324 --> 00:13:09,364
Now takes twenty years instead of seventeen.

259
00:13:09,824 --> 00:13:10,324
Progress.

260
00:13:10,804 --> 00:13:11,624
Reform bills?

261
00:13:11,864 --> 00:13:12,404
Tried.

262
00:13:12,444 --> 00:13:13,724
Lobbyists killed them in committee.

263
00:13:14,224 --> 00:13:14,804
Efficiently.

