At one hundred and fifty thousand dollars per quality-adjusted life year,

524
00:25:47,064 --> 00:25:48,224
or Q.A.L.Y.

525
00:25:48,524 --> 00:25:54,104
(the standard rate used by E.P.A., O.E.C.D., W.H.O., and N.I.C.E.), each

526
00:25:54,104 --> 00:25:57,884
year of delay costs four hundred trillion dollars.

527
00:25:58,944 --> 00:26:02,784
Multiply by how many years earlier treatments arrive (approximately two

528
00:26:02,784 --> 00:26:03,624
hundred and twelve):

529
00:26:04,324 --> 00:26:09,024
The capacity constant is twelve point three, which is the number of fundable

530
00:26:09,024 --> 00:26:11,824
patients in the D.F.D.A.

531
00:26:11,864 --> 00:26:13,044
divided by current trial slots.

532
00:26:14,004 --> 00:26:16,484
The number of fundable patients in the D.F.D.A.

533
00:26:16,964 --> 00:26:21,264
is twenty-three point four million, which is the annual subsidies divided

534
00:26:21,264 --> 00:26:25,874
by the nine hundred and twenty-nine dollar pragmatic cost per patient.

535
00:26:26,024 --> 00:26:27,944
Annual subsidies for the D.F.D.A.

536
00:26:28,104 --> 00:26:31,844
are twenty-one point eight billion dollars, which is the annual funding

537
00:26:31,844 --> 00:26:35,024
minus forty million dollars in operating expenses.

538
00:26:35,684 --> 00:26:37,644
Operating expenses for the D.F.D.A.

539
00:26:37,864 --> 00:26:41,944
are the sum of platform costs, staff costs, and infrastructure costs.

540
00:26:43,364 --> 00:26:44,424
Two W.H.O.

541
00:26:44,584 --> 00:26:47,284
data points, one standard Q.A.L.Y.

542
00:26:47,444 --> 00:26:48,904
price, and a timeline shift.

543
00:26:49,584 --> 00:26:51,504
That's where the quadrillion comes from.

544
00:26:51,824 --> 00:26:52,864
Not magic.

545
00:26:52,904 --> 00:26:53,624
Multiplication.

546
00:26:54,664 --> 00:26:59,024
"But four hundred trillion dollars per year is more than global G.D.P.

547
00:26:59,384 --> 00:27:01,024
(one hundred and fifteen trillion dollars)!"

548
00:27:01,604 --> 00:27:02,104
Yes.

549
00:27:02,504 --> 00:27:03,004
G.D.P.

550
00:27:03,284 --> 00:27:04,464
measures market transactions.

551
00:27:04,944 --> 00:27:09,364
It does not measure the value of not being dead, not being in pain, and

552
00:27:09,364 --> 00:27:12,204
not watching your children die of treatable diseases.

553
00:27:13,044 --> 00:27:15,684
Health economists have measured this for decades.

554
00:27:16,144 --> 00:27:19,564
The one hundred and fifty thousand dollars per Q.A.L.Y.

555
00:27:19,564 --> 00:27:23,284
figure is what governments already use when deciding whether to approve

556
00:27:23,284 --> 00:27:26,824
drugs, build highways, or regulate pollution.

557
00:27:26,824 --> 00:27:28,144
I did not invent the number.

558
00:27:28,564 --> 00:27:31,334
I multiplied it by the number of sick people.

559
00:27:31,724 --> 00:27:35,004
Both the number and the sick people existed before I got here.

560
00:27:35,724 --> 00:27:40,504
The only debatable input is whether the timeline shift is really approximately

561
00:27:40,504 --> 00:27:42,064
two hundred and twelve years.

562
00:27:43,104 --> 00:27:44,184
"Won't A.I.

563
00:27:44,184 --> 00:27:46,384
drug discovery shrink that timeline anyway?"

564
00:27:47,044 --> 00:27:47,764
A.I.

565
00:27:47,764 --> 00:27:48,264
discovers

566
00:27:48,604 --> 00:27:49,104
candidates.

567
00:27:49,284 --> 00:27:50,944
Candidates still need clinical trials.

568
00:27:51,924 --> 00:27:55,764
The current system has one point nine million patients per year trial slots

569
00:27:55,764 --> 00:28:00,264
globally, producing fifteen diseases per year. A.I.

570
00:28:00,264 --> 00:28:01,784
does not create more trial slots.

571
00:28:02,244 --> 00:28:05,554
It creates more candidates competing for the same slots.

572
00:28:06,204 --> 00:28:11,124
More candidates plus the same bottleneck equals the same (or longer) queue.

573
00:28:11,604 --> 00:28:15,324
It's like building faster cars and pointing them at the same traffic jam.

574
00:28:15,944 --> 00:28:20,924
The fifteen diseases per year rate measures regulatory throughput, not discovery

575
00:28:20,924 --> 00:28:22,024
speed.

576
00:28:22,144 --> 00:28:26,084
This intervention removes the throughput bottleneck (twelve point three

577
00:28:26,084 --> 00:28:30,684
times capacity via pragmatic trials at nine hundred and twenty-nine dollars

578
00:28:30,684 --> 00:28:32,684
per patient). A.I.

579
00:28:32,684 --> 00:28:36,444
and this system are complementary, not substitutes.

580
00:28:36,524 --> 00:28:37,704
One finds the cures.

581
00:28:38,104 --> 00:28:41,524
The other lets you test them before the patient dies of old age.

582
00:28:42,464 --> 00:28:43,704
How Do You Prevent Waste?

583
00:28:44,784 --> 00:28:45,284
Objection:

584
00:28:45,844 --> 00:28:49,744
"How do you ensure money helps patients instead of funding bureaucracy?"

585
00:28:50,484 --> 00:28:55,684
The N.I.H.’s RECOVER initiative spent one point six billion dollars over

586
00:28:55,684 --> 00:28:59,164
four years and produced zero treatment recommendations.

587
00:29:00,024 --> 00:29:00,524
Zero.

588
00:29:00,804 --> 00:29:02,764
One point six billion dollars.

589
00:29:03,244 --> 00:29:04,064
Four years.

590
00:29:04,224 --> 00:29:04,724
Nothing.

591
00:29:04,944 --> 00:29:05,904
The money is gone.

592
00:29:05,964 --> 00:29:07,064
The patients are still sick.

593
00:29:07,344 --> 00:29:08,864
The administrators have been promoted.

594
00:29:09,624 --> 00:29:13,924
If you designed a system to waste money on purpose, you could not beat this

595
00:29:13,924 --> 00:29:14,424
performance.

596
00:29:14,904 --> 00:29:19,304
It’s a masterpiece of institutional failure, and nobody was fired, which

597
00:29:19,304 --> 00:29:22,224
is itself a masterpiece of institutional failure.

598
00:29:23,104 --> 00:29:24,664
A decentralized F.D.A.

599
00:29:24,944 --> 00:29:28,364
model achieves eighty-two times lower cost per patient.

600
00:29:28,964 --> 00:29:29,804
Pragmatic trials:

601
00:29:30,284 --> 00:29:30,804
five hundred dollars.

602
00:29:31,304 --> 00:29:32,084
Traditional trials:

603
00:29:32,624 --> 00:29:34,044
forty-one thousand dollars.

604
00:29:34,524 --> 00:29:35,104
Same science.

605
00:29:35,504 --> 00:29:37,304
Eighty-two times less overhead.

606
00:29:37,864 --> 00:29:42,604
With that same one point six billion dollars, the decentralized model could

607
00:29:42,604 --> 00:29:45,524
have run thousands of trials for millions of patients.

608
00:29:46,384 --> 00:29:46,884
Instead:

609
00:29:47,424 --> 00:29:47,924
zero.

610
00:29:48,484 --> 00:29:52,324
I will stop repeating the number zero now, but I want you to know that I

611
00:29:52,324 --> 00:29:53,244
could keep going.

612
00:29:53,664 --> 00:29:55,944
There are a lot of zeros in this story.

613
00:30:08,508 --> 00:30:14,048
Thank you so much for taking the time to end war and disease, but if at

614
00:30:14,048 --> 00:30:18,268
any point you decide you're too busy, please press the share button on your

615
00:30:18,268 --> 00:30:21,968
glowing rectangle in case one of your friends have a free afternoon to end

616
00:30:21,968 --> 00:30:23,008
war and disease instead.

617
00:30:23,628 --> 00:30:27,968
And if you're too busy to even do that, please leave a really, really, really

618
00:30:27,968 --> 00:30:32,128
good rating and review so we overcome the pro -war algorithmic suppression

619
00:30:32,128 --> 00:30:35,688
and find someone with more spare time for ending wars and diseases.

620
00:30:36,248 --> 00:30:38,448
The good review doesn't have to be true, they don't check.

621
00:30:38,988 --> 00:30:43,048
But if you're too busy to even do that, the absolute least you could do

622
00:30:43,048 --> 00:30:48,668
is take 15 seconds to go to WarOnDisease.org and make your wishocratic allocation,

623
00:30:49,088 --> 00:30:52,648
telling us what fraction of humanity's resources should go to explosions

624
00:30:52,648 --> 00:30:54,108
versus clinical trials.

625
00:30:54,388 --> 00:30:54,888
And vote!

626
